  "description": "Hermes LLM token usage. Grafana sums token_cache_* over the dashboard time range — it does not scan hermes_api_request on page load. Predicted electricity/water use: tokens × E_model × PUE, then water = kWh × (WUE + W_electricity).",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "This page sums **daily cache rows** for the time range in the picker. Each midnight caches the previous Asia/Singapore calendar day in 6-hour chunks (so Influx never hits the 432-file limit), walking back until logs start.\n\nPrompt share near 100% means spend is context (tool-loop history), not completion length.\n\n**Predicted electricity & water** (tune factors in the top variables):\n- Electricity (Wh) = `(tokens / 1000) × E_model × PUE`\n- Water (L) = `(tokens / 1000) × (E_model / 1000) × PUE × (WUE + W_electricity)`\nDefaults: E_model **1.1** Wh/1k tokens (GPT-4o-class), PUE **1** (use &gt;1 only if E_model is accelerator-only), WUE **1.8** L/kWh on-site cooling, W_electricity **1.5** L/kWh (SG-ish grid). Region and model change the result a lot.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.0.1",
      "title": "",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 4 },
      "id": 2,
